# Claude credentials for ONE VPS.
#
# The real file lives only on your home machine, at
#   ~/.config/fleet/secrets/<node>/claude.env      (for example .../secrets/vps1/claude.env)
# `fleet init` creates it from this template. It leaves your PC only through
#   fleet secrets push claude <node>
# which copies it to that VPS (~/.config/fleet/providers/claude.env, readable by
# the fleet user only). Never commit the real file.
#
# Fill in ONE of the two. If both are set, Claude Code uses the API key, so leave
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY empty when you use a subscription token.
#
# A) The fleet's default: a Claude Pro or Max subscription token, with a separate
#    Claude account for each VPS. On your PC run `claude setup-token`, sign in with
#    the Claude account this VPS uses, and paste the token here. It is valid for one
#    year; `fleet health` reminds you a month before it expires. When the account
#    reaches its 5-hour or weekly usage limit, this VPS starts no new jobs until the
#    limit resets, then resumes the interrupted Claude session where it stopped.
#    Read docs/providers/claude-accounts.md (Anthropic's rules) before you start.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
#
# B) A Claude Console API key instead: billed per use, no 5-hour or weekly limits,
#    and the option Anthropic recommends for business use. Create one per VPS at
#    https://platform.claude.com (API keys), so each VPS can have its own spend limit.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
#
# Optional settings for every job on this VPS (a job's own fields win):
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
# CLAUDE_MAX_TURNS=
# CLAUDE_PERMISSION_MODE=bypassPermissions
